274
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:06,160
Chiffon, even if it's only for a moment.

275
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:09,640
I heard she got married.

276
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,018
I only want to give her my blessing.

277
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,520
Have mercy on this old soul.

278
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:17,839
If I can talk to Linlin,
we can work something out.

279
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:21,180
I overheard a rumor that Lola ran away.

280
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:23,140
You don't understand.

281
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:26,000
I worry about my precious children.

282
00:18:26,980 --> 00:18:27,810
Lola, huh?

283
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,576
She's your daughter?

284
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:34,457
One of my older sisters did the latter.

285
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:38,740
She ran off to see a while
back in search of a husband.

286
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,160
Of her choosing.

287
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:45,557
You said that she ran away.

288
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:48,477
Rekker let go of me.

289
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:52,157
I only want to see my
daughters is that so wrong.

290
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:55,700
I promise I'll never
ask for anything else.

291
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,530
Lola.

292
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:01,077
She must be...

293
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,480
Wow, Lola.

294
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:04,917
I didn't realize you went
to the New World already.

295
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,817
We didn't go there, you big silly.

296
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:08,417
We came from there in the first place.

297
00:19:08,500 --> 00:19:10,971
My mama's a pirate just like me, you know?

298
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:13,300
Oh, that reminds me.

299
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:15,540
Here, you should take this.

300
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:17,171
It's my mama's Viva card.

301
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:19,560
A piece of paper? Whoa!

302
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:21,017
I hang on to that one.

303
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:24,837
One of the greatest pirates I've
ever met in my life was Lola's mom.

304
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,437
That'll come in handy someday.

305
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,579
Not just anybody gets one of those.

306
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:33,408
Everything makes sense now.

307
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:35,880
No way.

308
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:39,620
Lola told us that her mom was a pirate.

309
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,660
So it was Big Mom?

310
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:48,480
I can't believe it.

311
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:52,780
This guy, he's Lola's father.

312
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,500
Those two are back!

313
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,197
It's the bird and rabbit guy!

314
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,456
And it's flying now?

315
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:28,020
Randolph, hold!

316
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,100
Wait a sec, was that Haki?

317
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,887
Well, what else could it be?

318
00:21:03,180 --> 00:21:05,100
They all screamed in terror.

319
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,440
And then withered away?

320
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:31,970
Randolf

321
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:42,117
Interrupting my entrance
and getting in the

322
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:45,320
way you must think you're
a real big shot now!

323
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,560
Well, Randolph?

324
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,240
My apologies. It was his idea.

325
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:53,617
That's a blatant lie!

326
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:54,759
This one's on you!

327
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:57,320
They can talk?

328
00:21:57,840 --> 00:21:59,140
Please forgive us!

329
00:22:01,580 --> 00:22:04,227
They're acting like he
holds a high position.

330
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:07,940
He's strong, that's for sure.

331
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:12,737
You know that Mama always likes
to stay ahead of the curve,

332
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:16,600
considering Straw Hat Luffy was
the man who beat Doflamingo.

333
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:19,337
She assumed Barrel would have a hard time,

334
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:25,040
So she sent me did my ears hear
that correctly brother dear?

335
00:22:44,040 --> 00:22:44,997
She's back, huh!

336
00:22:45,080 --> 00:22:48,717
If she had ordered me to kill
them, I would have off them by now.

337
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,180
Exactly right!

338
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:52,640
We, the Seducing Wood's team,

339
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,697
would have never allowed
a single assigned target!

340
00:22:55,780 --> 00:22:57,540
to leave this forest alive!

341
00:22:58,300 --> 00:22:59,130
Golly!

342
00:22:59,213 --> 00:23:02,337
Not only did Barrel and Cranker
show up here, but King Palme, too!

343
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:03,250
Wow!

344
00:23:03,333 --> 00:23:06,417
It's hard to believe they're all
in the woods at the same time!

345
00:23:06,500 --> 00:23:07,760
That's just dandy.

346
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:10,314
But we have little time for your games.

347
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:14,160
By tomorrow at noon,

348
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,477
the Vinsmoke siblings will be
arriving at the Whole Cake Shit?

349
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:19,640
making time a precious commodity.

350
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:23,977
Forming a family connection
with the Vinsmooks has been

351
00:23:24,060 --> 00:23:27,178
a long-awaited goal that
Mama's been working towards.

352
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:38,840
She'll finally obtain Germa Double Six's
military might and scientific expertise.

353
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:40,980
I realize that.

354
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,440
He turned into animals!

355
00:23:58,540 --> 00:23:59,400
Hold up.

356
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:01,500
How can that tree talk?

357
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:03,460
What did you just call me?

358
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:05,820
Tell me, can a tree do this, huh?

359
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:08,940
Luffy! Luffy!

360
00:24:09,540 --> 00:24:11,260
Luffy, come and send us free!

361
00:24:12,440 --> 00:24:13,920
She caught Chopper, too?

362
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,720
What happened, you guys?

363
00:24:15,940 --> 00:24:17,411
How did you get in there?

364
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:20,020
She trapped us both in this mirror world.

365
00:24:20,260 --> 00:24:23,520
She can use a tricky
ability, so be careful.

366
00:24:26,180 --> 00:24:28,415
How do you like that, Brother Cracker?

367
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:32,220
I've got these fools
right where I want them.

368
00:24:33,340 --> 00:24:35,340
By the scruff of their neck.

369
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:50,120
No, what happened?

370
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:52,220
Answer me! Are you okay?

371
00:24:54,940 --> 00:24:55,877
We're fine.

372
00:24:55,960 --> 00:24:57,600
It didn't hurt us.

373
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:00,340
It was only the mirror that broke.

374
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:04,019
Nothing bad happened to us
here in the mirror world.

375
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:05,700
What a relief.

376
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:08,726
I don't get it, but
that's good news at least.

377
00:25:08,960 --> 00:25:10,160
Luffy, listen.

378
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:13,480
I'm wasting time.

379
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:17,195
First off, I'd better deal
with this loose-lipped fool.

380
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:19,031
What do you mean by that?

381
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:20,591
What are you going to do?

382
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:22,680
She said that I'm to kill you.

383
00:25:29,020 --> 00:25:31,000
Can you reconsider, please?

384
00:25:31,420 --> 00:25:33,714
We can still talk this through, Gregor.

385
00:25:33,900 --> 00:25:36,677
Remember, I'm your stepdaughter after all.

386
00:25:36,760 --> 00:25:39,060
In the past, yes, but not anymore.

387
00:25:40,140 --> 00:25:44,357
Mama herself considers her 43
ex-husbands practically strangers.

388
00:25:44,440 --> 00:25:47,760
To us, you're no longer
family and no longer blood.

389
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:50,480
Oh, how can you say that?

390
00:25:50,620 --> 00:25:53,397
Telling me I'm no longer
related to my own daughters.

391
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:55,100
I can hardly bear it.

392
00:25:55,280 --> 00:25:57,100
I promise, no funny business.

393
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:59,889
I only want to give
them my blessing, okay?

394
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:16,880
Ah!

395
00:26:19,020 --> 00:26:19,940
Ah!

396
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:36,499
Was that sympathy?

397
00:26:37,180 --> 00:26:41,320
When you run into someone again
and again, you get attached!

398
00:26:47,540 --> 00:26:49,260
Oh, thank you!

399
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:51,640
Really, thank you!

400
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:11,300
This is about to get ugly!

401
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,657
General Cracker's gonna stop that guy!

402
00:27:13,740 --> 00:27:15,564
And maybe ask while he's at it!

403
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:19,487
Omasa, seize them so we can make
sure the job gets done right!

404
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:21,540
We should run!

405
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:22,838
It's not safe here!

406
00:27:24,160 --> 00:27:24,990
Let's go!

407
00:27:28,240 --> 00:27:30,260
You can leave the tower, Splay!

408
00:27:30,640 --> 00:27:31,980
Don't let them escape!

409
00:27:37,180 --> 00:27:38,857
What's your name, by the way?

410
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:40,800
You can just call me Bound!

411
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:47,200
About earlier, it sounded
like you know Lola.

412
00:27:47,500 --> 00:27:48,997
I do, but...

413
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:50,120
Hold on a sec.

414
00:27:56,020 --> 00:27:56,960
Here we go.

415
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:06,880
What have you got?

416
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:08,957
It's a present from my buddy Lola.

417
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:12,017
A piece of her mother's
beaver card, or so she said.

418
00:28:12,100 --> 00:28:12,930
What?

419
00:28:13,013 --> 00:28:14,620
I assume that's Big Mom.

420
00:28:18,520 --> 00:28:19,700
What are you doing?

421
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:21,626
What's come over, all of you?

422
00:28:23,040 --> 00:28:24,560
Even you, King Baum?

423
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:26,172
Tell me what's going on.

424
00:28:26,620 --> 00:28:27,800
We can't proceed.

425
00:28:28,100 --> 00:28:28,980
Sorry, mule.

426
00:28:30,060 --> 00:28:32,060
Homies can't disoccupy her.

427
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,220
It's tree, son.

428
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,460
And why's that?

429
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:38,720
The sense mama's soul
and can't shrub it off.

430
00:28:51,260 --> 00:28:53,740
This must be Big Mom's beaver card.

431
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:54,840
I had a hunch.

432
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:56,240
Just look at them.

433
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,860
Whoa, Luffy!

434
00:29:09,180 --> 00:29:10,060
Are you okay?

435
00:29:18,780 --> 00:29:19,880
Oh, no.

436
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:21,395
He's headed this way.

437
00:29:23,780 --> 00:29:26,820
He grew worms? Damn it!

438
00:29:28,180 --> 00:29:29,980
This guy sucks!

439
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:36,720
I am the Biscuit Knight Cracker, one
of Big Mom's Sweet Three Generals.

440
00:29:38,260 --> 00:29:40,000
You shall learn to respect.

441
00:29:40,780 --> 00:29:42,980
Thousand-armed cracker, Straw Hat.

442
00:29:43,320 --> 00:29:47,560
By simply tapping like so,
I can grow another arm.

443
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:50,140
Tap twice and I get three.

444
00:29:52,340 --> 00:29:55,040
I'm sure you get the picture. Huh?

445
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,120
However, that's not all.

446
00:30:04,360 --> 00:30:05,317
No way!

447
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,280
Legs, too?

448
00:30:07,780 --> 00:30:10,980
You couldn't even beat me
in your wildest dreams.

449
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:14,400
You fools will not interfere
with Mama's tea party.

450
00:30:14,660 --> 00:30:16,120
Extra limbs won't help.

451
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:17,820
Now, second gear.

452
00:30:21,140 --> 00:30:23,700
Hulk bust us all the arms you've got.

453
00:30:24,220 --> 00:30:26,740
Come, come, get bullet.

454
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:31,120
And another one.

455
00:30:31,760 --> 00:30:33,700
Come, come, Hulk whip.

456
00:30:42,260 --> 00:30:45,160
Luffy, you can't turn
this into an Alto fight.

457
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:47,108
We need to get out of here.

458
00:30:47,340 --> 00:30:50,458
Let's find Sanji so we can
leave this demented place.

459
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:54,820
Everything I do is all out.

460
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:58,000
Sorry, but it's the only way I know.
